# Ebb — Seats

## Contract

The seat contract — what a seat is, its lifecycle, seat accounting, the rules, launching, and the standing prompt — is `contracts/SEATS.md` in the template repo, copied verbatim into `wheelhouse/fleet/SEATS.md` at install. It is not reproduced here, and it is not edited per-project.

This specimen shows only what the interview writes: the roster below, and the seats that were offered and turned down.

## This project

### Seat namespace

`ebb` — seat root `$HOME/.claude-seats-ebb`, and the prefix every seat name below
carries. Derived once at the install interview and recorded as `namespace=ebb`
in `wheelhouse/.template-source`, which is where `wire-seats.sh` reads it. This
line and that one must say the same string; `.template-source` is the copy a
program acts on, so it is the one that decides.

### Roster

| Seat | Role brief | Account | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `ebb-worker-1` | `wheelhouse/fleet/WORKER.md` | `ebb-fleet-1` | Primary implementation |
| `ebb-reviewer` | `wheelhouse/crew/REVIEWER.md` | `ebb-fleet-2` | Never authors what it reviews |
| (commander) | this folder's `CLAUDE.md` | (principal's own) | The principal's own session |

### Declined seats

| Seat | Reason | Date |
|---|---|---|
| Designer | "I want to decompose the first few beads myself so I learn what a good one looks like." | 2026-08-14 |
| Second worker | One reviewer, one worker — take it when the reviewer starts waiting. | 2026-08-14 |

Each of these was offered seat by seat at install and turned down. A second worker goes in when the reviewer is idle waiting for work; the designer goes in when the principal is spending more time decomposing beads than deciding direction.

---

## What the installed file actually looks like

This specimen shows only the generated half. The file at `wheelhouse/fleet/SEATS.md` in a real project is:

```
# Fleet: Seats
<intro line>

## Contract                 <- copied verbatim from contracts/SEATS.md, never edited
  ### What a seat is
  ### Lifecycle             <- context is a cache; ephemeral default, standing is a promotion
  ### Seat accounting       <- one seat = one subscription = one human beneficiary
  ### Rules
  ### Launching a seat
  ### Standing prompt
  ### Minimum viable fleet

## This project             <- everything from here down is generated, and is the
  ### Seat namespace           only part this specimen shows
  ### Roster
  ### Declined seats
```

If your installed file is missing the contract half, the install split it in the wrong place. That has happened; see the note in `BOOTSTRAP.md` about matching the heading exactly.
